{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXefCqidmJtRLtjXZ92b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a plan based on what I have about Mila:\n\n**What she wants:** something quiet, just the two of you, no crowds. She likes small jazz gigs. She has a serious peanut allergy, and you've said to skip Thai and Indian places.\n\n**The evening of Wed 11 Nov**\n1. **Dinner for two, early.** Pick a small, quiet restaurant, with a reservation for a corner table. Tell them about the peanut allergy when you book. Italian, French or Japanese are safer than most, but still ask about cross-contamination. Cooking at home is also an option. It's the only way to control the allergen fully, and it fits \"just you and me\".\n2. **Jazz, if you can find it.** The Bluebird trio she likes plays Saturdays at 9, so it doesn't land on Wednesday. Check whether they have a Wednesday slot. If not, you could take her to the Bluebird on Sat 7 Nov or Sat 14 Nov as part of the celebration. Otherwise, put on a jazz record at home with a good bottle.\n3. **Small touch:** a gift or note that shows you remembered the details, like her favorite flowers or a dessert from a bakery you've checked is peanut-free.\n\n**Logistics**\n- Mother-in-law Vesna arrived around 26 Oct for two weeks, so she may still be with you in early November. I'm not sure of the exact dates. If she's still there on the 11th, you may want to arrange a quiet hour out of the house.\n- You said November is filling up. I'd block the evening of the 11th now, and Sat 7 or 14 Nov if you want the Bluebird.\n- You asked for reminders one week before (**4 Nov**) and the day before (**10 Nov**). I can't set them from here, but I can schedule them if you want.\n\nDo you want me to shortlist quiet restaurants near you? If so, tell me the city and a budget. Also tell me whether you'd rather go out or stay in."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_de